# Diagnostics table of the GPU-code frontend - the single source of the GPU#### codes (REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md, 3.3).
#
# This is data shared by future frontends (ASM, Rust): code, severity, message and hint are not hard-coded in
# Java code. It is packaged into the resources of the frontend-java module. Codes are stable: their meaning does
# not change, numbers are not reused.
#
# Line format:   <code> <error|warning> <message> | <hint>
#   {0}, {1}, ... - substituted values (method name, type, etc.); the hint may be empty.
#
# Groups:  GPU00xx - declarations and annotations (signatures, attributes, fallback)
#          GPU01xx - constructs and types in method bodies (the Java subset for GPU)
#          GPU02xx - compilation environment
#          GPU09xx - internal errors (IR validation, frontend failure); report them as a library bug

# --- declarations and annotations ---------------------------------------------------------------
GPU0001 error   Method {0} with @{1} must be static | Add the static modifier
GPU0002 error   Method {0} with @Kernel must return void | Return the result through an array parameter
GPU0003 error   Invalid type {0} of parameter {1} | Allowed: int, long, float, double and one-dimensional arrays of primitive types
GPU0004 error   Parameter {0} of type boolean is not allowed | Use int (0 or 1) or a boolean[] array
GPU0005 error   Multidimensional arrays are not supported: {0} | Use a one-dimensional array and compute the index manually
GPU0006 error   Invalid result type {0} of device function {1} | Allowed: void, boolean, int, long, float, double
GPU0007 error   Method {0} cannot be generic, have a varargs parameter or declare throws | Remove type parameters, varargs and throws
GPU0008 error   Kernel {0} has its work-group size set both in @WorkGroup and in workgroup | Keep only one way
GPU0009 error   Unknown capability {0} in required of kernel {1} | Allowed: FP64, INT64_ATOMICS, FP16, IMAGES
GPU0010 error   fallback {0} of kernel {1} not found among the @Kernel methods of this class | Specify the name of a @Kernel method from the same class
GPU0011 error   fallback {0} has a different signature than kernel {1} | Parameter types and order must match
GPU0012 error   optLevel {0} of kernel {1} is outside the range 0..3 | Specify a value from 0 to 3
GPU0013 error   Work-group size must be positive on every axis: {0} | Specify x, y, z greater than zero
GPU0014 error   The fallback chain is cyclic: {0} | fallback must not refer to a kernel that is already in the chain
GPU0015 error   Field {0} with @Constant must be static final of a primitive type with a constant value | Set a constant expression in the initializer
GPU0016 error   Method {0} with @Reduction must return int, long, float or double | Return the accumulator of the loop
GPU0017 error   Method {0} has both @Kernel and @Reduction | Keep one of them
GPU0018 error   Method {0} is not a reduction: {1} | Write the body as: declarations; T acc = init; for (int i = start; i < end; i++) { acc += e; } return acc;

# --- constructs and types in method bodies ------------------------------------------------------
GPU0101 error   Exceptions are not supported in GPU code ({0}) | Remove try/catch/finally/throw; return errors as values
GPU0102 error   synchronized is not supported in GPU code | A barrier will be used for synchronization within a group
GPU0103 error   assert is not supported in GPU code | Remove the assert or replace it with a conditional check
GPU0104 error   Labels (labeled break/continue/statement) are not supported | Rewrite using a boolean flag and plain break/continue
GPU0105 error   Recursion is forbidden: {0} | Rewrite iteratively
GPU0106 error   Strings are not supported in GPU code | Use numeric codes
GPU0107 error   Objects are not supported in GPU code: {0} | GPU code allows primitives and one-dimensional arrays of primitives
GPU0108 error   Lambdas, method references and local or anonymous classes are not supported | Move the logic into a method with @DeviceFunction
GPU0109 error   Invalid cast or instanceof: {0} | Casts between primitive numeric types are allowed
GPU0110 error   The switch construct is not supported: {0} | A switch statement over int, short, byte or char with constant labels is allowed
GPU0111 error   The for-each loop is not supported | Use a for loop with an index
GPU0112 error   Method {0} is not supported in GPU code | Use the Gpu.* builtins or methods with @DeviceFunction
GPU0113 error   The called method {0} is not marked @DeviceFunction | Add @DeviceFunction (a kernel cannot be called from GPU code)
GPU0114 error   The source code of method {0} is unavailable: device functions from libraries without sources are not supported yet | Compile together with the module that has the processor
GPU0115 error   Invalid access to field {0} | Only local variables, parameters and constants (static final) are allowed
GPU0116 error   Invalid use of an array: {0} | An array can be indexed, its length taken, and passed as a parameter
GPU0117 error   Invalid array creation: {0} | Only 'T[] a = new T[constant];' in a local variable declaration is allowed
GPU0118 error   Assignment to parameter {0} with @Global(constant = true) | Copy the value into a local variable
GPU0119 error   Type {0} is not supported in GPU code | Allowed: boolean, byte, short, char, int, long, float, double and one-dimensional arrays of primitives
GPU0120 error   An array with @Local is allowed only in a kernel, at the top level of the body, with a constant size | Declare 'T[] a = new T[N];' at the start of the kernel
GPU0121 error   Address space mismatch of array {0}: the function expects {1}, passed {2} | Pass an array of the same address space (@Global, @Local)
GPU0122 error   Write to an element of array {0} with @Global(constant = true) | A constant array is read-only: copy the value into a @Global array
GPU0130 warning The barrier in kernel {0} may not be reached by all work-items of the group: {1} | The barrier must be placed where the whole group arrives; if the condition is the same for the group, wrap it in Gpu.assumeUniform(...)
GPU0131 error   The barrier in kernel {0} is under divergent control flow (strictBarriers mode): {1} | Move barrier() out of the condition that depends on getGlobalId/getLocalId, or wrap the condition in Gpu.assumeUniform(...)
GPU0191 error   Invalid @Struct declaration {0}: {1} | Fields are public, not final: int, long, float, double, vectors or other @Struct; a public no-arg constructor is required
GPU0192 error   Invalid creation of object {0}: {1} | Create a vector with a constructor over all components, and a @Struct with a constructor over all fields
GPU0193 error   The struct value {0} must be created by a new expression or copy(), not taken from a variable | Use 'new P(...)' or 'x.copy()': on the GPU a struct is copied, on the JVM it would be a shared reference
GPU0194 error   Invalid write to field {0}: {1} | Change fields of a local struct variable or of a struct array element; a struct parameter is read-only
GPU0195 error   The shuffle index must be a constant within 0..{0} | Specify literal numbers or constants (static final)
GPU0196 error   Comparing objects {0} is not allowed | Compare components (x, y, ...) or fields
GPU0197 error   A pointer is not allowed in kernel parameters {0}: {1} | Pass an array; create the pointer in the body: GlobalFloatPtr.of(array, offset)
GPU0198 error   Invalid use of pointer {0}: {1} | FloatPtr reference: new in a declaration, .value and passing to @DeviceFunction; GlobalFloatPtr pointer: of, get, set, plus
GPU0199 error   Pointer {0} is created from an array of address space {1}, but an array of address space {2} was passed | Use a pointer matching the address space of the array (Global/Local/Constant)

# --- compilation environment --------------------------------------------------------------------
GPU0201 error   Failed to get access to the javac Tree API from {0} | Compile with javac (ECJ is not supported); report your environment if this is javac

# --- internal errors ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GPU0901 error   The IR of kernel {0} failed validation: {1} | Internal frontend error or an IR contract violation; report it with a code sample
GPU0902 error   Internal frontend error while processing {0}: {1} | Report it with a code sample
GPU0903 warning IR of kernel {0}: {1} |
